      "@type": "bootstrap:Skill",
      "ambiguous": false,
      "description": "Read what changed on main often, and re-analyse the session workplan. Put main INTO the branch rarely: freely before a PR exists, and on a branch with a PR only when it conflicts, when the work needs something that just landed, or once just before it merges, because each such push re-runs the PR's whole CI. Prevents stale assumptions, merge conflicts, and duplicated work without spending CI on churn.",
